<ontology/use_cordage_shipbuilding/use_cordage_shipbuilding__0289__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. HEMP" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Hemp Rough or Undressed used in Shipbuilding, Rope, Cordage & Sailcloth: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. HEMP"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "HEMP: (Chanvre, Fr.; Hanf, Germ.) is the fibrous rind of the bark of the cannabis sativa, which is spun into strands or yarn for making ropes, sail-cloth, &c. It is prepared for spinning in the same way as flax, which see. Hemp-seed contains an oil which is employed for making soft soap, for painting, and for burning in lamps. See OILS. Importation of undres..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
